--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Licensing exception: kernel/linux/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The optional Linux kernel module under kernel/linux/ is dual licensed
MIT OR GPL-2.0-only, not Apache-2.0. It is written in Rust, like the rest of
the project, but the licence is a constraint the kernel imposes. The kernel accepts only a fixed set of
MODULE_LICENSE idents and none of them is Apache; anything outside that set
taints the kernel on load and loses access to GPL-only symbols. Apache-2.0 is
also generally held to be incompatible with GPLv2, which the kernel is.

That directory shares no source with the rest of the project and communicates
only through a text file in /proc, so the boundary is clean. The module is
optional: nothing in the toolkit requires it.

