--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software links the following dependencies, which carry their own terms.
Redistributing a NanoChronometer binary means redistributing these too; their
license texts must accompany it. See docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the full
release layout.

  ring                  Apache-2.0 AND ISC AND OpenSSL
                        The crypto provider. Contains code derived from
                        BoringSSL, which carries the OpenSSL and ISC licenses;
                        see the LICENSE files in the ring crate.

  rustls                Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT
  rustls-webpki         ISC
  rustls-pki-types      Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  webpki-roots          MPL-2.0
                        Mozilla's root certificate set, redistributed as data.

  libc                  Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  windows-sys           Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  clap                  Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  ctrlc                 Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  tokio                 MIT
  iced                  MIT
                        Desktop GUI only; not linked into the libraries, the
                        CLI, or any Android artifact.
  image                 MIT OR Apache-2.0
                        Desktop GUI only. Already present through iced; named
                        directly so the ICO decoder is enabled explicitly
                        rather than by whatever features another crate
                        happened to turn on.
  winresource           MIT
                        Windows builds only, and build-time only: it invokes
                        the resource compiler to put the application icon into
                        the .exe. Nothing from it is linked into any binary,
                        so it is not redistributed.

  sha2, hmac, aes-gcm,  Apache-2.0 OR MIT (RustCrypto)
  chacha20poly1305      Bare-metal kernel only, for its RustCrypto benchmark.
  cpufeatures 0.2.17    Apache-2.0 OR MIT (RustCrypto)
                        Vendored and modified in
                        crates/nanochrono-baremetal/vendor/cpufeatures/: it
                        reports every feature absent when target_os is "none",
                        and the copy detects them there instead (CPUID on x86,
                        the EL1 ID registers on AArch64). Its LICENSE-APACHE
                        and LICENSE-MIT are kept beside the source.

Run `cargo tree --format "{p} {l}"` for the complete, version-exact list.
